          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
            induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group+law"} formal group law
            from its first
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conner-Floyd+Chern+class"} Conner-Floyd Chern class
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen%27s+theorem+on+MU"} Quillen's theorem on MU
            together with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lazard%27s+theorem"} Lazard's theorem
            say that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+ring"} cohomology ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet(M U)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+cobordism+cohomology"} complex cobordism cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MU"} MU
            is the classifying ring for formal group laws.
          %p
            Conversely, the
            %em Landweber exact functor theorem
            (
            %a{:href => "#Landweber76"}> Landweber 1976
            ) says that forming the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+cobordism+cohomology+theory"} complex cobordism cohomology theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MU"}> MU
            ) with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Landweber+exactness"} Landweber exact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            via some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group+law"} formal group law
            yields a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
          %p
            By the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} Brown representability theorem
            this defines a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            and the spectra arising this way are called
            = succeed "." do
              %em Landweber exact spectra
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie17"} e.g. Lurie 2017, lect 17, p.2
          %p
            There is an analogue of the statement also for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+cohomology+theory"} even
            2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/periodic+cohomology+theories"}> periodic cohomology theories
            , with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MU"} MU
            replaced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MP"} MP
            (
            %a{:href => "#LurieLect18"}> Lurie lecture 18, prop. 11
            ).
          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
            By evaluation on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X =
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BU%28n%29"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundles"} complex line bundles
            (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+2-group"} circle 2-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theory"} multiplicative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            gives rise to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group"} formal group
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+ring"} graded ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet(E)
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "complex+oriented+cohomology+theory#FormalGroupLaw"} there
          %p
            Conversely, given a formal group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+ring"} graded ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            in this way.
          %p
            Now since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lazard+ring"} Lazard ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            classifies formal groups, in that any formal group law
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+ring"} ground ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is equivalently a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \longrightarrow R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen%27s+theorem+on+MU"} Quillen's theorem on MU
            identifies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+ring"} cohomology ring
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi MU
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \simeq MU_\bullet(\ast)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi MU
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munder
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi L
                  %mi R
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \mapsto E_\bullet(X) \coloneqq MU_\bullet(X) \underset{L}{\otimes} R
                  \\,.
          %p
            By construction this is such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\bullet(\ast) \simeq R
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+homology+theory"} generalized homology theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} Brown represented
            by an actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
            Landweber exactness is a sufficient condition on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi MU
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi L
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \coloneqq MU_\bullet(-)\otimes_L R
            to be indeed a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+homology+theory"} generalized homology theory
            (e. g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#LurieLecture15"} Lurie, lect 15, theorem 9
          %p Notice that if it is, then the canonical map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi MU
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi MU
                        %mo •
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  MU_\bullet(X) \otimes_{MU_\bullet} E_\bullet \stackrel{}{\longrightarrow} E_\bullet(X)
          %p
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            this was originally proven in
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#ConnerFloyd66"} Conner-Floyd 66
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex orientation
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+theory+determining+homology+theory"} cobordism theory determining homology theory
          %h2#properties_of_landweberexact_spectra Properties of Landweber-exact spectra
          %h3#phantom_maps Phantom maps
          %p
            Between Landweber exact spectra, every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phantom+map"} phantom map
            is already null-homotopic. (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie"} Lurie lect 17, corollary 7
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              The special case of the Landweber exact functor theorem for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+topological+K-theory"} complex topological K-theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
              is known as the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conner-Floyd+isomorphism"} Conner-Floyd isomorphism
          %h2#related_theorems Related theorems
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lazard%27s+theorem"} Lazard's theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+complex+orientation+on+MU"} universal complex orientation on MU
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen%27s+theorem+on+MU"} Quillen's theorem on MU
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Landweber-Novikov+theorem"} Landweber-Novikov theorem
          %h2#references References
          %p
            For the special case of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            the statement (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Conner-Floyd+isomorphism"}> Conner-Floyd isomorphism
            ) is originally due to:
          %ul
            %li#ConnerFloyd66
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Conner"}> Pierre Conner
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edwin+Floyd"} Edwin Floyd
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Relation+of+Cobordism+to+K-Theories"} The Relation of Cobordism to K-Theories
              %strong 28
              Springer 1966 (
              %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/BFb0071091"}> doi:10.1007/BFb0071091
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=216511"} MR216511
          %p
            The general result for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology"} complex oriented cohomology
            is due to:
          %ul
            %li#Landweber76
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Landweber"}> Peter Landweber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Homological properties of comodules over
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi MU
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi MU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU^\ast(MU)
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi BP
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi BP
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BP^\ast(BP)
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2373808"} jstor:2373808
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#TamakiKono06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dai+Tamaki"}> Dai Tamaki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akira+Kono"} Akira Kono
              = succeed "," do
                %em Generalized Cohomology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/mmono-230"} ISBN: 978-0-8218-3514-2
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li#LurieLecture15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chromatic+Homotopy+Theory"} Chromatic Homotopy Theory
                %em
                  Flat modules over
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℳ
                          %mi FG
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{FG}
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/252xnotes/Lecture15.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chromatic+Homotopy+Theory"} Chromatic Homotopy Theory
                %em The Landweber exact functor theorem
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/252xnotes/Lecture16.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Lurie17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chromatic+Homotopy+Theory"} Chromatic Homotopy Theory
                %em Phantom maps
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/252xnotes/Lecture17.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Landweber_exact_functor_theorem"} Landweber exact functor theorem
          %p For the even 2-periodic case:
          %ul
            %li#LurieLect18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chromatic+Homotopy+Theory"} Chromatic Homotopy Theory
              %em Even periodic cohomology theories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/252xnotes/Lecture18.pdf"}> pdf
              )
